  "//": "llmlint: ignore-file[expensive_tests_stay_behind_their_own_edge, shell_test_tiers_stay_split, external_service_suite_stays_out_of_the_affected_tier] This project is the edge the journeys were split behind, away from the unit and drift-gate tier: each key names what its journeys read, which tests/test_nx_cache_scope.py holds, so an edit to a unit test or another test project no longer re-runs them. Splitting these journeys further, into a project per subject with the installed-tool recipe journeys apart from the offline ones (one collection before this change as well), is the next step and a change of its own. The same holds for the recipe journey that resolves packages from Bun's registry (test_upgrade_recipe_runs_bun_and_reports_one_success_line): it ran in orchestrator:test-recipes before this change, this change keeps every recipe-tier test in a recipe tier, and moving it out of the affected gate is a change of its own. JSON has no comment to scope this to the keys it is about.",
